<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Raise Skeleton</h1>
<p>Sphere: Creation Sphere
Class: Necromancer (guild level 50)
Mana: 20
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cast raise skeleton &lt;corpse&gt;
tell skeleton &lt;command&gt;
tell horde &lt;command&gt;     (all your undead at once)
</pre>
<p>The necromancer cuts themself, bleeds upon a corpse and chants 'Sine 
muera aneme', and its flesh turns to dust as a skeletal warrior rises from 
the bones. The skeleton is as strong as a zombie (see <a cmd='#'>Help Animate 
Dead</a>); for a far stronger servant, see <a cmd='#'>Help Raise Skeletal Champion</a>. It 
follows its maker and carries what the corpse held.
</p><p>Command it with tell, just as with <a cmd='#'>Help Animate Dead</a>. It lasts a few 
minutes, up to a quarter of an hour or more for a master, then crumbles 
to dust, leaving what it carried. A strong dispel magic ends it sooner. It 
never attacks players, unless both you and they have signed the Book of 
Blood.
</p><p>Only corpses of monsters will rise: a player's corpse won't. Corpses of 
insects and other crawling things, of the undead, demons and devils, 
elementals, golems, gargoyles and the like crumble to dust instead. You 
must be standing, and no free hands are needed. It is also found on 
wands, staffs and scrolls.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Animate Dead</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Raise Skeletal Champion</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Raise Horde</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Necromancer Spells</a>
</pre>




</div>